<!--
  ats_invalid_accented_razon_social.xml — razonSocial carries a non-ASCII letter.

  Rule exercised: razonSocialType, ats.xsd:41-52. Its pattern at ats.xsd:50 is
  "[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9\s]+[a-zA-Z0-9\s]", which admits only ASCII letters,
  digits and whitespace. "ñ" is outside that class, so the document is rejected.

  Element under test: iva/razonSocial, ats.xsd:598.
  This fixture breaks the rule twice over: the accented "ñ" and the "." of
  "S.A." are both outside [a-zA-Z0-9\s]. denoProvType ats.xsd:1501-1507 carries
  the identical restriction, so the same stripping applies to the supplier name.

  Consequence for the builder: the accent stripper is mandatory, not cosmetic.
-->
